<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4388" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλη</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλᾳ</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλᾷ</span></b>  (as <i><span class="en">
			A.D.
			<u>Adv.</u>
			175.13
		</span></i>), Delph. and Megar. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>GDI</u>
					1830
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				3052
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Chalcedon</span>), Adv.,
			properly dat. fem. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλος</span>:
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of Place,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>elsewhere</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				23
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.36
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				4.28
			</span></i>: c. gen. loci, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλος ἄ. τῆς
				πόλεως</span> one <i>in one part of</i> the city, one
				<i>in another</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τῆς κεφαλῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VC</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλοτε ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					1.5.20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. καὶ ἄ.</span>
			<i>here</i> and <i>there</i>, prob. l. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.2.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to another place, elsewhither</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.187
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.288
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρχεται ἄ.</span>, i.e. is
				<i>lost</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.120
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλοι ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.46
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτ᾽ ἐπὶ θήρην ἰοῦσαι οὔτ᾽ ἄ.
					οὐδαμῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.114
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of Manner,
				<i>otherwise</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.51
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ τε ἄ. πολλαχῆ
			καὶ</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. γέ πῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					189c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.1.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
